CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal


Preamble

CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among
hardware designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the
freedom to use, study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs
and products based on those designs. Version 2 of the CERN Open
Hardware Licence comes in three variants: CERN-OHL-P (permissive); and
two reciprocal licences: CERN-OHL-W (weakly reciprocal) and this
licence, CERN-OHL-S (strongly reciprocal).

The CERN-OHL-S is copyright CERN 2020. Anyone is welcome to use it, in
unmodified form only.

Use of this Licence does not imply any endorsement by CERN of any
Licensor or their designs nor does it imply any involvement by CERN in
their development.


1 Definitions

  1.1 'Licence' means this CERN-OHL-S.

  1.2 'Compatible Licence' means

       a) any earlier version of the CERN Open Hardware licence, or

       b) any version of the CERN-OHL-S,

       or

       c) any licence which permits You to treat the Source to which
          it applies as licensed under CERN-OHL-S provided that on
          Conveyance of any such Source, or any associated Product You
          treat the Source in question as being licensed under
          CERN-OHL-S.

  1.3 'Source' means information such as design materials or digital
      code which can be applied to Make or test a Product or to
      prepare a Product for use, Conveyance or sale, regardless of its
      medium or how it is expressed. It may include Notices.

  1.4 'Covered Source' means Source that is explicitly made available
      under this Licence.

  1.5 'Product' means any device, component, work or physical object,
      whether in finished or intermediate form, arising from the use,
      application or processing of Covered Source.

  1.6 'Make' means to create or configure something, whether by
      manufacture, assembly, compiling, loading or applying Covered
      Source or another Product or otherwise.

  1.7 'Available Component' means any part, sub-assembly, library or
      code that:

       a) is licensed to You as Complete Source under a Compatible
          Licence; or

       b) is available, at the time a Product or the Source containing
          it is first Conveyed, to You and any other prospective
          licensees

            i) as a physical part with sufficient rights and
               information (including any configuration and
               programming files and information about its
               characteristics and interfaces) to enable it either to
               be Made itself, or to be sourced and used to Make the
               Product; or
           ii) as part of the normal distribution of a tool used to
               design or Make the Product.

  1.8 'Complete Source' means the set of all Source necessary to Make
      a Product, in the preferred form for making modifications,
      including necessary installation and interfacing information
      both for the Product, and for any included Available Components.
      If the format is proprietary, it must also be made available in
      a format (if the proprietary tool can create it) which is
      viewable with a tool available to potential licensees and
      licensed under a licence approved by the Free Software
      Foundation or the Open Source Initiative. Complete Source need
      not include the Source of any Available Component, provided
      that You include in the Complete Source sufficient information
      to enable a recipient to Make or source and use any Available
      Components to Make the Product.

  1.9 'Source Location' means a location where a Licensor has placed
      Covered Source, and which that Licensor reasonably believes will
      remain easily accessible for at least three years for anyone to
      obtain a digital copy.

  1.10 'Notice' means copyright, acknowledgement and trademark notices,
       Source Location references, modification notices (subsection 3.3(b))
       and all notices that refer to this Licence and to the disclaimer of
       warranties that are part of the Covered Source.

  1.11 'Licensee' or 'You' means any person exercising rights under
       this Licence.

  1.12 'Licensor' means a natural or legal person who creates or
       modifies Covered Source. A Licensor may also be a Licensee.

  1.13 'Convey' means to communicate to the public or distribute.

  1.14 'Upstream Component' means a component that You receive from a
       Licensor as part of the Covered Source, with the exception of
       a component that is an Available Component.

  1.15 'User Product' means a Product that is sold or otherwise made
       available for use by consumers in the course of normal
       operations.

  1.16 In this Licence, 'patent licence' means an express agreement or
       commitment, however denominated, not to enforce a patent
       (such as an express permission to practise a patent or a
       covenant not to sue for patent infringement).


2 Applicability

  2.1 This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, Conveying
      of Covered Source and Products, and the Making of Products. By
      exercising any right granted under this Licence, You irrevocably
      accept these terms and conditions.

  2.2 This Licence is granted by the Licensor directly to You, and
      shall apply worldwide and without limitation in time.

  2.3 You shall not attempt to restrict by contract or otherwise the
      rights granted under this Licence to other Licensees.

  2.4 This Licence is not intended to restrict fair use, fair dealing,
      or any other similar right.


3 Copying, Modifying and Conveying Covered Source

  3.1 You may copy and Convey verbatim copies of the Covered Source in
      any medium, provided You retain all Notices.

  3.2 You may modify the Covered Source, other than Notices, provided
      that You irrevocably undertake to make that modified Source
      available in the same way as the Covered Source for at least
      three years from the date it is first Conveyed, and in any
      event for as long as you Convey the modified Source, and to
      make it available to anyone who requests it (either directly or
      through a third party). You must also make a copy of this
      Licence available to them.

  3.3 You shall, in the modified Source, carry all Notices as follows:

       a) retaining the notice of any prior licensor to the extent
          required by that licensor;

       b) adding a notice stating that You have modified the Source,
          with the date and brief description of how You have modified
          it.

  3.4 You may Convey compiled or processed forms of the Covered Source,
      including as a Product, provided that You also Convey the
      Complete Source of the Covered Source in the same way as You are
      required to Convey the Complete Source of modified Source under
      subsection 3.2, with the following exception: if the Covered
      Source is compiled or processed to make it directly executable on
      target hardware, the Complete Source may instead be Conveyed via
      a Source Location, provided that You include in that compiled or
      processed form the information necessary to find the Source
      Location.

  3.5 Either conditionally or unconditionally, You may Convey the
      Covered Source with or without modification, in conjunction with
      a Product.


4 Making and Conveying Products

You may Make Products, and/or Convey them, provided that You ensure
that the recipient of the Product receives a copy of the Complete
Source, a copy of this Licence, and that You comply with subsection
3.3 with regard to any Notices in the Covered Source.


5 Research and Development

You may Convey Covered Source or Products to a legal entity carrying
out development, testing or quality assurance work on Your behalf
provided that all such work is carried out solely for Your use,
and such entity undertakes to disclose any such Source or Products to
You should there be any improvement or change, and You undertake to
make any such disclosed Source or Products available under this
Licence.


